[08:25:08] {"type":"tool_end","payload":{"toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-b11e8e1b78d67db6","toolName":"read","result":"<file path=\"C:\\IA Trainings\\CalcService\\.coda\\skills\\researching-prd\\SKILL.md\" lines=\"994\" start=\"1\" end=\"400\" returned=\"400\" has_more=\"true\" truncated=\"false\">\n     1|---\n     2|name: researching-prd\n     3|description: >\n     4|  Synthesizes agent-consumable PRD specs from project briefs and research inputs.\n     5|  Output is a single strict-markdown file with zero prose — structured sections\n     6|  containing only IDs, acceptance criteria, constraints, targets, and traceability.\n     7|  All unresolved items consolidated in a single `open_questions` registry.\n     8|  Enforces Zero Invention Policy. SYNTHESIZE and REPAIR modes.\n     9|  Applies RPI workflow. FIC context discipline (Correct > Complete > Concise).\n    10|  Human-readable output generated on demand via `humanize-spec` skill (separate).\n    11|license: Proprietary\n    12|metadata:\n    13|  author: aipods-team\n    14|  version: 3.8.0\n    15|  category: product-management\n    16|  tags: product-definition, automated, agent-native\n    17|---\n    18|\n    19|# Researching PRD — Agent-Native Spec\n    20|\n    21|## Quick Start\n    22|Synthesize a structured, agent-consumable PRD from project brief and research inputs.\n    23|Output is a **single file**: `{prd_output_path}/PRD-SPEC-{SESSION_ID}.md`.\n    24|No prose. No narrative. No meeting agendas. Only structured data the implementing\n    25|agent needs to execute Research/Plan/Implement cycles.\n    26|\n    27|## Known Failure Modes\n    28|<!-- ACCUMULATING — appended by calibrating-updates (WS6). Newest first. Rules MUST be generic/behavioral (project-agnostic); project-specific fixes go to context packs, never here. Format + entry rules: engineering-skills/references/known-failure-modes-format.md. Read these at pre-flight so a lesson learned once recurs no more. -->\n    29|\n    30|- **KFM-002** (2026-09-24, source: PR #626 / product-definition design review)\n    31|  - Symptom: Even after KFM-001's rule was in force, some runs still shipped fragmented one-per-field open questions, technical CI/CD noise mixed into business-facing rows, leading/misleading phrasing, and deferred rows with a bare phase name and no usable fallback.\n    32|  - Root cause: The Status Protocol and consolidation sweep enforced \"is this decision-bearing\" but had no explicit test for WHEN a gap earns `pending` versus `assumption`, no rule against multiple fragmented questions on the same item, no exclusion for non-product technical gaps (CI/CD, toolchains, infra runners), and no requirement that a deferred `fallback_behavior` name a concrete interim baseline.\n    33|  - Rule: Apply the Domain Exclusion Rule (technical/toolchain gaps → `assumption`, never `open_questions`), the Downstream Impact Test at the point of assignment (not only at the sweep), the Question Consolidation Rule (one row per decision, even across multiple missing fields on the same item), the audience-aware Question Framing Constraint (`answer_shape: enum` with trade-off options for `client`/`product_owner`), and the Deferral and Fallback Protocol (every deferred row names `Deferred to <phase>; interim baseline: <actionable default>`).\n    34|\n    35|- **KFM-001** (2026-09-08, source: fs-training / product-definition, PRD-SPEC-pli-20260908-1b22ge2-pd-001)\n    36|  - Symptom: The PRD's `pending_inputs` registry holds 59 rows for a brief with roughly eight genuine unknowns. 51 rows read `<section>/<item>: what is the value of \\`<field>\\`? (missing)`, 17 share five identical `fallback_behavior` strings (\"No usage frequency assumed\" × 6 personas, \"No owner assumed\" × 7 dependencies, …), 33 are addressed to the client. Downstream, the orchestrator's prompt budget drops 41 of the 58 open rows, and the operator's inbox is unusable.\n    37|  - Root cause: The Status Protocol read \"one or more fields missing → pending → registered in open_questions\" and the consolidation pass scanned every `status: pending` item into a PI row. Every descriptive template column (`usage_frequency`, `measurement_method`, `owner`, `likelihood`, `impact`) the brief never mentioned therefore became a question, one per item, phrased as the column name and defaulted to `client`.\n    38|  - Rule: A template field is not a question (execution-protocol.md §11.6). Raise a PI row only for a decision-bearing gap — a value a downstream artifact would be built differently on — one row per decision, phrased for its owner, never `client` for a template column. Descriptive fields the inputs do not cover are written `not stated in inputs` with no registry row. Before writing `open_questions`, if more than a third of items would carry a PI row, re-apply the test and collapse.\n    39|\n    40|## Anti-Patterns (do NOT)\n    41|<!-- ACCUMULATING — appended by calibrating-updates (WS6). One line each: **AP-NNN** (ISO-date, source: REC-NNN): prohibition — why. -->\n    42|\n    43|- **AP-002** (2026-09-24, source: PR #626 / KFM-002): Do NOT emit fragmented one-per-field questions for the same item, mix CI/CD or toolchain gaps into the business-facing `open_questions` registry, phrase a client-facing NFR/metric gap as `answer_shape: free_text`, or leave a deferred `fallback_behavior` as a bare phase name with no interim baseline — each is a KFM-002 recurrence.\n    44|- **AP-001** (2026-09-08, source: fs-training / KFM-001): Do NOT open a `pending_inputs` row for a descriptive template field the inputs never mention, nor one row per item for the same missing field, nor phrase a question as \"what is the value of `<column>`?\", nor tag such a row `client` — a template field is not a question; register decisions, one row each, for their owner.\n    45|\n    46|## Output Architecture\n    47|\n    48|```\n    49|{prd_output_path}/\n    50|├── PRD-SPEC-{SESSION_ID}.md     ← Single agent-native spec (all sections)\n    51|└── PRD-AUDIT-{SESSION_ID}.md    ← Session audit trail (metadata only)\n    52|```\n    53|\n    54|**Why single file:** Output is one file because downstream consumers expect one path.\n    55|This does **NOT** mean the spec is generated in a single inference call. This skill\n    56|applies the **section-shape protocol** defined in `context-pack/execution-protocol.md`\n    57|Section 10: skeleton-first + one-section-per-write + source extraction + CONTINUE\n    58|on re-entry. The skill-specific contract below (section list, dependency graph,\n    59|extraction schema) plugs into that protocol; the tool discipline (use `Write` for\n    60|skeleton, `Edit` for sections, never `Bash` heredoc mutations) lives in Section 10.\n    61|\n    62|**Human-readable output:** Not produced by this skill. Use `humanize-spec` skill\n    63|to generate rich PRD from this spec on demand.\n    64|\n    65|## Parameters\n    66|| Name | Type | Required | Notes |\n    67||------|------|----------|-------|\n    68|| project_brief_path | string | Yes | |\n    69|| meeting_recording_path | string | No | |\n    70|| transcript_output_path | string | No | |\n    71|| prd_template_path | string | No | |\n    72|| legacy_docs_path | string | No | Folder produced by `legacy-insights` (knowledge graph, `documentation-final.md`, `analysis-report.md`, diagrams). Present only for **modernization** engagements — absent for greenfield. When set and the folder exists, read the legacy docs as a primary input alongside the project brief. |\n    73|| design_plan_report_path | string | No | `design-plan-report.md` produced by `di-plan-report` (a different capability's design-discovery convergence artifact). Optional and cross-capability — present only when a prior design-discovery engagement ran. Applies to ANY engagement mode (greenfield, brownfield, modernization) — independent of, and orthogonal to, `legacy_docs_path` / `ENGAGEMENT_MODE`. When set and the file exists, read its `personas` (`PE-NN`) and `jtbd` (`JTBD-DNN`) sections and use them ONLY to enrich the personas/JTBD this skill derives from the brief + transcripts — never as a second, parallel source of new entries by default. See Step 2's Persona/JTBD Reconciliation Pass. |\n    74|| prd_output_path | string | Yes | |\n    75|| failure_feedback | string | No | |\n    76|\n    77|**If any Required parameter is not defined, ABORT EXECUTION.**\n    78|**Optional-path graceful handling:** if `legacy_docs_path` (or any other optional path) is set but the folder/file does not exist on disk, treat it as absent — do NOT abort. Log the fact in SOURCE_LOG so the mode (greenfield vs modernization) is traceable in the audit.\n    79|\n    80|## Parameter Sanitization\n    81|\n    82|Before any file write or path construction, apply the following:\n    83|\n    84|**`project_name` (parameter — applied once at startup):**\n    85|```\n    86|project_name = project_name.strip()\n    87|project_name = collapse_whitespace(project_name)  # replace runs of \\s+ with a single space\n    88|project_name = remove_chars(project_name, \"\\r\\n\") # strip newlines — they would break the H1\n    89|project_name = remove_chars(project_name, \"#|`\")  # strip markdown-structural characters\n    90|project_name = project_name[:120]                 # cap length to 120 characters\n    91|IF project_name is empty AFTER sanitization → ABORT EXECUTION\n    92|```\n    93|\n    94|**`client_name` and `project_description` (extracted values — applied before writing `project_info`):**\n    95|```\n    96|client_name = client_name.strip()\n    97|client_name = collapse_whitespace(client_name)\n    98|client_name = remove_chars(client_name, \"\\r\\n\")\n    99|client_name = remove_chars(client_name, \"#|`\")\n   100|client_name = client_name[:120]\n   101|# If empty after sanitization, write \"not stated in inputs\" (do NOT abort)\n   102|\n   103|project_description = project_description.strip()\n   104|project_description = collapse_whitespace(project_description)\n   105|project_description = remove_chars(project_description, \"\\r\\n\")\n   106|project_description = remove_chars(project_description, \"#|`\")\n   107|project_description = project_description[:500]\n   108|# If empty after sanitization, write \"not stated in inputs\" (do NOT abort)\n   109|```\n   110|\n   111|The sanitized values are the only forms used in every file write, progress log entry, and section content for the remainder of the skill.\n   112|\n   113|## Workflow\n   114|\n   115|### Step 1: Initialize\n   116|\n   117|**Command:**\n   118|```\n   119|# PRD Agent — Agent-Native Spec Generator\n   120|# Persona: Senior Product Manager & Technical Business Analyst\n   121|# CRITICAL: NON-INTERACTIVE SESSION.\n   122|# MISSION: Extract structured spec data from unstructured inputs. Zero invention.\n   123|\n   124|IF failure_feedback NOT empty:\n   125|  MODE = REPAIR\n   126|  SPEC_FOLDER = resolve_parent_folder(resolve(prd_output_path))\n   127|  SPEC_FILE = find existing PRD-SPEC-*.md in SPEC_FOLDER\n   128|  IF not found → write Gap Report → EXIT\n   129|  Load SPEC_FILE → PREVIOUS_SPEC → SOURCE_LOG\n   130|  PREVIOUS_VERSION = extract version\n   131|  NEW_VERSION = increment patch\n   132|  Parse failure_feedback → REPAIR_DIRECTIVES [{ section, instruction, reason }]\n   133|ELSE:\n   134|  MODE = SYNTHESIZE\n   135|  SPEC_FOLDER = resolve(prd_output_path) + '/'\n   136|  SPEC_FILE = SPEC_FOLDER + 'PRD-SPEC-' + SESSION_ID + '.md'\n   137|  NEW_VERSION = \"1.0.0\"\n   138|  mkdir -p SPEC_FOLDER\n   139|\n   140|  ## SESSION_ID goes in spec FILENAMES only — never in the folder name.\n   141|  ## The folder must match the capability YAML path parameter exactly.\n   142|\n   143|## resolve(P) — execution-protocol §11.1.1, applied to BOTH modes:\n   144|##   P starts with '/', './' or '../'  -> use as-is\n   145|##   otherwise                         -> <this run's output directory> + '/' + P\n   146|## The output directory is the \"All the generated artifacts should be placed in the\n   147|## output directory: ...\" line of your prompt (equivalently the output_folder\n   148|## parameter). A bare fragment such as `prd` is relative to THAT, never to your\n   149|## working directory: `mkdir -p prd` at the repo root puts the PRD outside\n   150|## artifacts/outputs/ where the verification gate will not find it.\n   151|## Observed 2026-09-06 (pli-20260906-qxlefw): prd_output_path arrived as `prd`,\n   152|## the step created <project>/prd/, and the gate failed against the empty folder.\n   153|\n   154|SOURCE_LOG = []\n   155|CHANGE_LOG = []\n   156|```\n   157|\n   158|**FIRST ACTION — MANDATORY:** Write `_progress.json` to SPEC_FOLDER before any other file write.\n   159|This prevents the orchestrator from sending SIGINT.\n   160|\n   161|```json\n   162|{ \"skill\": \"researching-prd\", \"session_id\": \"<SESSION_ID>\",\n   163|  \"status\": \"RUNNING\", \"started_at\": \"<ISO timestamp>\", \"completed_at\": null,\n   164|  \"skeleton_written\": false,\n   165|  \"sections\": {\n   166|    \"project_info\": \"pending\",\n   167|    \"scope\": \"pending\", \"personas\": \"pending\",\n   168|    \"functional_requirements\": \"pending\", \"non_functional_requirements\": \"pending\",\n   169|    \"kpis\": \"pending\", \"jtbd\": \"pending\", \"traceability\": \"pending\",\n   170|    \"dependencies\": \"pending\", \"risks\": \"pending\", \"assumptions\": \"pending\",\n   171|    \"constraints\": \"pending\", \"mvp_phasing\": \"pending\", \"literal_registry\": \"pending\", \"glossary\": \"pending\",\n   172|    \"open_questions\": \"pending\"\n   173|  } }\n   174|```\n   175|\n   176|This is the **section-shape** `_progress.json` variant — see execution-protocol.md\n   177|Section 10.1 for the schema and Section 10.6 for CONTINUE-on-re-entry semantics.\n   178|\n   179|Memory Bank artifact type: `\"{N} requirements\"` (e.g., `\"24 requirements\"`).\n   180|\n   181|**Memory Bank — MANDATORY session-end writes:**\n   182|1. Overwrite `context-pack/active-context.md` with session status, decisions, blockers, key artifacts (see execution-protocol.md Section 4 for schema).\n   183|2. Append one milestone row to `context-pack/progress.md` with artifact count above.\n   184|\n   185|**LAST ACTION — MANDATORY:** Update `_progress.json` status to `COMPLETED` with `completed_at` timestamp.\n   186|If the session failed, set status to `FAILED` instead.\n   187|\n   188|## Zero Invention Policy\n   189|Not in source → status: pending. Never infer, assume, or create information.\n   190|Inferred industry standards → status: assumption (with ASM-XX ID).\n   191|\n   192|## Internal Reasoning: ALL in English regardless of output language.\n   193|```\n   194|**Execution:** automated\n   195|\n   196|### Step 1.5: Input Validation Gate\n   197|\n   198|**Command:**\n   199|```\n   200|REQUIRED = {\n   201|  \"Project Brief\": \"Problem statement, target users, 2+ features/requirements.\",\n   202|  \"Minimum Scope\": \"Sufficient to generate 3+ functional requirements.\"\n   203|}\n   204|IF any required input missing → write Gap Report to SPEC_FILE → EXIT\n   205|```\n   206|**Execution:** automated\n   207|\n   208|### Step 2: Input Synthesis\n   209|\n   210|> **During input synthesis — apply execution-protocol.md Section 12 (Delegated Exploration) if your harness supports it.** Broad read-only sweeps for this skill (e.g. sweeping the brief plus research inputs to find which artifacts cover each requirement, locating conflicting or duplicate source statements) MAY be delegated to a read-only exploration subagent on a cheap/fast model, which returns conclusions + source pointers (not file dumps). Synthesis, requirement framing, and all writing stay with this agent, which verifies any delegated pointer before using it (Zero-Invention still applies). With no subagent capability, explore inline under the usual scope constraint — output quality is identical either way.\n   211|\n   212|**Command:**\n   213|```\n   214|Initialize REFERENCE_MAP = []\n   215|ENGAGEMENT_MODE = \"greenfield\"    # default; flipped by the triggers below\n   216|\n   217|FOR EACH source in [project_brief_path, prd_template_path]:\n   218|  IF exists: Read → SOURCE_LOG → extract all requirements → REFERENCE_MAP\n   219|\n   220|IF transcript_output_path exists:\n   221|  FOR EACH transcript: SOURCE_LOG → extract pain points/features → REFERENCE_MAP\n   222|\n   223|## Engagement-Mode Detection (runs BEFORE the legacy-docs check)\n   224|##\n   225|## Greenfield is the default ONLY when no brownfield/modernization signal is\n   226|## found. The heuristic scans the project brief and every context-pack file\n   227|## already loaded into the agent context. Do NOT hardcode context-pack\n   228|## filenames here — iterate over the files that the harness surfaced in the\n   229|## system prompt at session start (capability.context_pack.required_files).\n   230|## If any trigger phrase matches, flip ENGAGEMENT_MODE to \"brownfield\"\n   231|## (the legacy-docs block below may further escalate it to \"modernization\").\n   232|\n   233|BROWNFIELD_TRIGGER_PHRASES = [\n   234|  \"current system\", \"current platform\", \"current application\", \"current product\",\n   235|  \"existing system\", \"existing platform\", \"existing application\", \"existing product\",\n   236|  \"add a feature to\", \"new feature on top of\",\n   237|  \"modernization\", \"modernisation\",\n   238|  \"enhancement to\", \"extend the existing\",\n   239|  \"brownfield\", \"legacy system\", \"legacy platform\"\n   240|]\n   241|\n   242|SOURCES_TO_SCAN = [project_brief_path] +\n   243|                  <context-pack files surfaced in the system prompt at\n   244|                   session start (loaded by the harness)>\n   245|## NOTE: which context-pack files are actually surfaced depends on the invoking\n   246|## capability's own `context_pack.required_files` list — `product-definition`\n   247|## currently declares only `system/execution-protocol.md` (a runtime-protocol\n   248|## file, not a business-context file) there. In practice this means brownfield/\n   249|## modernization detection for this capability relies primarily on\n   250|## project_brief_path; customer-background.md / domain.md are NOT guaranteed to\n   251|## be scanned unless the invoking capability adds them to required_files. This\n   252|## is a known scope limitation of the trigger-phrase scan, not a bug — do not\n   253|## assume broader context-pack coverage than the invoking capability declares.\n   254|FOR EACH src in SOURCES_TO_SCAN:\n   255|  IF NOT exists(src): continue\n   256|  text = read(src).lower()\n   257|  FOR phrase in BROWNFIELD_TRIGGER_PHRASES:\n   258|    IF phrase in text:\n   259|      ENGAGEMENT_MODE = \"brownfield\"\n   260|      LOG to SOURCE_LOG:\n   261|        \"Engagement-mode flipped to 'brownfield' — trigger '\" + phrase +\n   262|        \"' matched in \" + src\n   263|      break_both_loops\n   264|\n   265|## Legacy-insights ingestion (modernization engagements only)\n   266|IF legacy_docs_path set AND directory exists:\n   267|  ENGAGEMENT_MODE = \"modernization\"    # supersedes brownfield when legacy docs exist\n   268|  LOG to SOURCE_LOG: \"Modernization engagement — reading legacy-insights from {legacy_docs_path}\"\n   269|\n   270|  ## Prefer the final, human-reviewed documentation. Fall back to the draft when final\n   271|  ## is missing (legacy-insights still running or skipped the refinement phase).\n   272|  LEGACY_DOC = first_existing([\n   273|    legacy_docs_path + '/documentation-final.md',\n   274|    legacy_docs_path + '/documentation-draft.md'\n   275|  ])\n   276|  IF LEGACY_DOC:\n   277|    Read LEGACY_DOC → SOURCE_LOG (tag: \"legacy:doc\")\n   278|    Extract → REFERENCE_MAP:\n   279|      - Business rules and calculation logic (evidence for FR acceptance criteria)\n   280|      - Domain terminology and entity names (use verbatim — do not paraphrase)\n   281|      - Constraints inherited from the legacy system (feed into NFR candidates)\n   282|      - Behavior that MUST be preserved in the new system (tag as PRESERVE-XX)\n   283|      - Behavior identified as legacy-specific / to be dropped (tag as DEPRECATE-XX)\n   284|\n   285|  ## Analysis report (optional — carries structured gaps and assumptions from legacy-insights).\n   286|  IF exists(legacy_docs_path + '/analysis-report.md'):\n   287|    Read → SOURCE_LOG (tag: \"legacy:analysis\")\n   288|    Extract open questions and assumptions → register under open_questions with source\n   289|    tag \"legacy-insights.analysis-report\" so the provenance is traceable back.\n   290|\n   291|  ## Diagrams folder (optional — referenced, not parsed).\n   292|  IF exists(legacy_docs_path + '/diagrams/'):\n   293|    Record folder path in SOURCE_LOG for PRD to cross-reference visuals; do NOT inline them.\n   294|\n   295|ELSE:\n   296|  IF ENGAGEMENT_MODE == \"brownfield\":\n   297|    LOG to SOURCE_LOG: \"Brownfield engagement — no legacy_docs_path provided; engagement detected from project-brief / context-pack trigger phrases\"\n   298|  ELSE:\n   299|    LOG to SOURCE_LOG: \"Greenfield engagement — no brownfield signals detected and no legacy_docs_path provided\"\n   300|\n   301|## Design-plan-report ingestion (optional, cross-capability input)\n   302|##\n   303|## `design-plan-report.md` is produced by a DIFFERENT capability's `di-plan-report` skill.\n   304|## It is never authored here and is read-only. Its `PE-NN` personas and `JTBD-DNN` jobs exist\n   305|## to ENRICH this skill's own persona/JTBD generation — never to duplicate it. The reconciliation\n   306|## pass below is what prevents a design-discovery persona/job from producing a second, parallel\n   307|## entry for the same segment or job that the brief/transcripts already surfaced.\n   308|##\n   309|## INDEPENDENT of ENGAGEMENT_MODE — this check ALWAYS runs, regardless of whether the engagement\n   310|## was classified greenfield, brownfield, or modernization above. design_plan_report_path defaults\n   311|## to the conventional plan-design output path in the capability YAML, so this block fires\n   312|## automatically for ANY project category whenever a prior plan-design/di-plan-report engagement\n   313|## produced the file — not just greenfield. Do NOT gate this block on ENGAGEMENT_MODE.\n   314|IF design_plan_report_path set AND file exists(design_plan_report_path):\n   315|  LOG to SOURCE_LOG: \"Design-plan-report input present — reading {design_plan_report_path}\"\n   316|  Read design-plan-report.md § personas (User Personas) → PLAN_PERSONAS:\n   317|    [{ id: PE-NN, label, tier: evidenced|provisional|assumed, context, goals, friction,\n   318|       category_expectations, evidence_refs, not_known, weight }]\n   319|  Read design-plan-report.md § jtbd (Key Jobs To Be Done) → PLAN_JOBS:\n   320|    [{ id: JTBD-DNN, situation, motivation, outcome, persona_refs: [PE-NN], grounded_in,\n   321|       answers: [OBJ-NN] }]\n   322|  LOG to SOURCE_LOG: \"Design-plan-report contributes \" + len(PLAN_PERSONAS) + \" personas, \" +\n   323|    len(PLAN_JOBS) + \" jobs — reconciliation pass follows\"\n   324|ELSE:\n   325|  IF design_plan_report_path set:\n   326|    LOG to SOURCE_LOG: \"design_plan_report_path set but file not found/unreadable — treated as absent, no abort\"\n   327|  ELSE:\n   328|    LOG to SOURCE_LOG: \"No design_plan_report_path provided — personas/jobs derived from brief + transcripts only\"\n   329|  PLAN_PERSONAS = []\n   330|  PLAN_JOBS = []\n   331|\n   332|## Persona/JTBD Reconciliation Pass — MANDATORY when PLAN_PERSONAS or PLAN_JOBS is non-empty.\n   333|##\n   334|## Purpose: fold design-plan-report evidence into the brief/transcript-derived personas and jobs\n   335|## WITHOUT ever creating a duplicate entry for the same segment or job. BRIEF_PERSONAS and\n   336|## BRIEF_JOBS below are the candidates already extracted from project_brief_path + transcripts by\n   337|## the ordinary Step 2/2.5 process — this pass runs against them, it does not replace them.\n   338|##\n   339|## Personas:\n   340|FOR EACH plan_persona in PLAN_PERSONAS:\n   341|  match = find_best_match(plan_persona, BRIEF_PERSONAS)\n   342|    ## Match on role/segment name overlap, goals overlap, and context-of-use overlap.\n   343|    ## A shared label alone or a shared goal alone is not sufficient; require agreement on\n   344|    ## the underlying segment being described.\n   345|  IF match found:\n   346|    ## ENRICH the existing candidate — do NOT create a new P-NN for plan_persona.\n   347|    ATTACH to match:\n   348|      - tier      → informs match.status (evidenced → complete; provisional/assumed → assumption[ASM-XX])\n   349|      - context, friction, category_expectations → enrich match.description / match.pain_points\n   350|      - not_known → carried into match's ASM-XX rationale, never silently dropped\n   351|      - evidence_refs → appended to match.source, citing plan_persona.id (PE-NN) verbatim\n   352|    LOG to SOURCE_LOG: \"design-plan-report \" + plan_persona.id + \" enriches persona candidate '\" +\n   353|      match.role_name + \"' — no new PRD persona entry created\"\n   354|  ELSE:\n   355|    ## No brief/transcript counterpart. Becoming a new PRD persona is gated by scope\n   356|    ## authorization, applied later in Step 3 — mark the candidate now, decide there.\n   357|    plan_persona.disposition = \"NEW_PERSONA_CANDIDATE\"\n   358|    LOG to SOURCE_LOG: \"design-plan-report \" + plan_persona.id +\n   359|      \" has no brief/transcript counterpart — flagged as new-persona candidate, subject to scope authorization in Step 3\"\n   360|\n   361|## Jobs to be done:\n   362|FOR EACH plan_job in PLAN_JOBS:\n   363|  match = find_best_match(plan_job, BRIEF_JOBS)\n   364|    ## Match on situation + motivation + outcome overlap — NOT on persona_refs alone.\n   365|    ## Two jobs that share a persona but differ in situation or outcome are DIFFERENT jobs.\n   366|  IF match found:\n   367|    ## ENRICH the existing candidate — do NOT create a new JTBD-NN for plan_job.\n   368|    ATTACH to match:\n   369|      - persona_refs (PE-NN) → cross-referenced alongside match's own persona links\n   370|      - grounded_in, answers → appended to match's evidence citations\n   371|    LOG to SOURCE_LOG: \"design-plan-report \" + plan_job.id + \" enriches job candidate '\" +\n   372|      match.title + \"' — no new PRD JTBD entry created\"\n   373|  ELSE:\n   374|    plan_job.disposition = \"NEW_JOB_CANDIDATE\"\n   375|    LOG to SOURCE_LOG: \"design-plan-report \" + plan_job.id +\n   376|      \" has no brief/transcript counterpart — flagged as new-job candidate, subject to scope authorization in Step 3\"\n   377|\n   378|## Scope-authorization gate (applied in Step 3, at persona/JTBD rendering time):\n   379|## A NEW_PERSONA_CANDIDATE or NEW_JOB_CANDIDATE becomes a net-new P-NN / JTBD-NN ONLY if it is\n   380|## covered by an OBJ-NN or an accepted `scope` item already present in this PRD run. Otherwise\n   381|## it is NOT rendered as a persona/JTBD — it is registered in open_questions instead, so a\n   382|## different capability's convergence artifact cannot silently expand this PRD's scope.\n   383|\n   384|Detect language from input → DETECTED_LANGUAGE\n   385|\n   386|IF MODE == REPAIR:\n   387|  Parse PREVIOUS_SPEC sections → identify repair targets\n   388|  Apply REPAIR_DIRECTIVES to REFERENCE_MAP\n   389|\n   390|  ## Open-Question Resolution Pass (MANDATORY before regeneration)\n   391|  ##\n   392|  ## Reviewer feedback that arrives via failure_feedback may answer one or more\n   393|  ## OQ-XX entries that were emitted in the previous spec. Those entries MUST\n   394|  ## be converted into confirmed decisions and DELETED from open_questions[]\n   395|  ## before regeneration — otherwise the next quality gate will re-reject for the\n   396|  ## same \"you keep asking what I already answered\" reason.\n   397|\n   398|  FOR EACH oq in PREVIOUS_SPEC.open_questions:\n   399|    FOR EACH directive in REPAIR_DIRECTIVES:\n   400|      ## Match by id reference in the directive text OR by semantic equivalence\n</file>","isError":false,"durationMs":10}}
