[08:25:32] {"type":"tool_start","payload":{"toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-b2e15f8f62324125","toolName":"read","args":{"path":"C:\\IA Trainings\\CalcService\\artifacts\\inputs\\project-brief.md","offset":1,"limit":300}}}
[08:25:32] {"type":"tool_end","payload":{"toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-b2e15f8f62324125","toolName":"read","result":"<file path=\"C:\\IA Trainings\\CalcService\\artifacts\\inputs\\project-brief.md\" lines=\"144\" start=\"1\" end=\"144\" returned=\"144\" has_more=\"false\" truncated=\"false\">\n     1|# **Project Brief: Math Operations Microservice (Calc-Service)**\n     2|\n     3|## Overview\n     4|\n     5|Calc-Service is a lightweight, stateless microservice that provides a centralized mathematical computation capability for the platform.\n     6|It externalizes calculation logic from client applications, enabling consistency, reuse, and controlled evolution of numerical behavior across the ecosystem.\n     7|\n     8|The service acts as a deterministic **math engine** that can be consumed by backend services, automation workflows, and AI-driven processes.\n     9|\n    10|---\n    11|\n    12|## **1. Business Objective**\n    13|\n    14|The goal is to deliver a reusable computation service that:\n    15|\n    16|* Eliminates duplicated calculation logic across systems\n    17|* Ensures consistent numerical precision\n    18|* Enables auditable calculation history when required\n    19|* Provides a stable foundation for future automation and AI orchestration\n    20|\n    21|The service supports both operational use cases (simple arithmetic) and analytical workflows (advanced math operations).\n    22|\n    23|---\n    24|\n    25|## **2. Core Capabilities**\n    26|\n    27|### **Standard Operations**\n    28|\n    29|* Addition\n    30|* Subtraction\n    31|* Multiplication\n    32|* Division\n    33|\n    34|### **Advanced Operations**\n    35|\n    36|* Exponentiation\n    37|* Roots\n    38|* Trigonometric functions\n    39|\n    40|### **Precision Strategy**\n    41|\n    42|* High-precision internal computation to reduce rounding inconsistencies\n    43|* Deterministic outputs suitable for financial and scientific contexts\n    44|\n    45|### **History Tracking (Optional)**\n    46|\n    47|* Records calculation metadata for traceability and diagnostics\n    48|* Implemented as lightweight local persistence\n    49|* Designed as auxiliary storage that must not impact response delivery\n    50|\n    51|### **Future Capability (Planned)**\n    52|\n    53|* Expression evaluation (e.g., `\"5 + (3 * 2)\"`)\n    54|* Workflow integration with automation agents\n    55|* Event-based history instead of database persistence\n    56|\n    57|---\n    58|\n    59|## **3. Architectural Positioning**\n    60|\n    61|Calc-Service follows a stateless microservice model:\n    62|\n    63|* Independent deployment\n    64|* Horizontally scalable computation layer\n    65|* Optional local persistence via embedded database abstraction\n    66|* No user session ownership\n    67|\n    68|The service is intentionally designed so persistence can be replaced without changing the API contract.\n    69|\n    70|Primary consumers include:\n    71|\n    72|* Backend services needing consistent math logic\n    73|* Reporting pipelines\n    74|* Automation workflows\n    75|* AI agents performing deterministic calculations\n    76|\n    77|---\n    78|\n    79|## **4. API Contract (Conceptual)**\n    80|\n    81|### **Calculate Operation**\n    82|\n    83|**Endpoint:** `POST /api/v1/math/calculate`\n    84|\n    85|**Input Example**\n    86|\n    87|```json\n    88|{\n    89|  \"operand1\": 10.5,\n    90|  \"operand2\": 5.0,\n    91|  \"operation\": \"ADD\"\n    92|}\n    93|```\n    94|\n    95|**Output Example**\n    96|\n    97|```json\n    98|{\n    99|  \"resultValue\": 15.5,\n   100|  \"operationType\": \"ADD\",\n   101|  \"timestamp\": \"2026-02-13T...\"\n   102|}\n   103|```\n   104|\n   105|### **History Retrieval (Optional)**\n   106|\n   107|Provides recent calculation records for diagnostics and auditing.\n   108|\n   109|---\n   110|\n   111|## **5. Non-Functional Goals**\n   112|\n   113|* **Determinism:** Same input always produces the same result\n   114|* **Latency:** Millisecond-level response time for standard operations\n   115|* **Reliability:** Calculation must succeed even if history persistence fails\n   116|* **Scalability:** Stateless design allows horizontal scaling\n   117|* **Observability readiness:** Designed for future metrics and tracing integration\n   118|\n   119|---\n   120|\n   121|## **6. Business Value**\n   122|\n   123|The service creates value by:\n   124|\n   125|* Reducing duplicated logic across teams\n   126|* Improving numerical consistency in decision processes\n   127|* Enabling auditability without coupling persistence to computation\n   128|* Serving as a foundational building block for AI-assisted workflows\n   129|\n   130|It establishes a single source of truth for mathematical behavior across the platform.\n   131|\n   132|---\n   133|\n   134|## **7. Success Criteria**\n   135|\n   136|* Service successfully integrated by at least one upstream system\n   137|* Deterministic unit test coverage for all operations\n   138|* Optional history persistence validated\n   139|* API contract documented for internal reuse\n   140|\n   141|---\n   142|\n   143|**Document Version:** 1.1\n   144|**Alignment:** Consistent with architecture standards, coding standards, and H2-based lightweight persistence strategy.\n</file>","isError":false,"durationMs":7}}
