[08:25:52] {"type":"tool_end","payload":{"toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-9fc92d590f06992b","toolName":"read","result":"<file path=\"C:\\IA Trainings\\CalcService\\.coda\\skills\\researching-prd\\references\\spec-template.md\" lines=\"432\" start=\"1\" end=\"400\" returned=\"400\" has_more=\"true\" truncated=\"false\">\n     1|# Agent-Native PRD Spec Template\n     2|\n     3|## Template Rules\n     4|- **No prose.** Every section is structured data only.\n     5|- **No narrative.** No \"why this matters\", no motivational text, no context paragraphs.\n     6|- **No formatting for humans.** No prominent text, no callouts, no visual emphasis.\n     7|  This governs DECORATION, not comprehension: a reference a reader cannot resolve is not\n     8|  \"agent-native\", it is unfinished. See **Name the thing, not just its id** below.\n     9|- **Name the thing, not just its id.** Exactly three fields are parsed as machine id\n    10|  lists and carry bare ids only: `affected_ids`, `applies_to_ids`, and the `id` column of\n    11|  any registry. EVERYWHERE ELSE an id appears — `traceability` cells, `mvp_phasing`,\n    12|  `sequencing_notes`, and every prose slot — the id is followed by the item's short name\n    13|  in parentheses: `FR-03 (job search by location)`. Take the name verbatim from that\n    14|  item's own definition heading; never paraphrase it differently in two places. A bare\n    15|  `FR-03` outside the machine fields is a defect, not a shorthand.\n    16|- **All items carry status.** `complete` | `pending` | `assumption`. This binds every\n    17|  bulleted line in every section, `scope` and `mvp_phasing` included — not only the\n    18|  requirement registries. Where an example below shows `| source: … | status: …`, that is\n    19|  the shape, not a suggestion.\n    20|- **All pending items appear in open_questions.** Single registry, no scatter. The\n    21|  consolidation sweep reads all fifteen prior sections, `scope` included — an unconfirmed\n    22|  item parked in `out_of_scope` is a pending input like any other.\n    23|- **Source tags are mandatory.** No source → cannot be `complete`.\n    24|- **Shape is copied, never recalled.** Header field list, headings, and table column sets\n    25|  come from this file at skeleton time (execution-protocol §10.3). Column names and their\n    26|  order are exact; a table renders with its full column set even when it has zero rows.\n    27|- **Empty is still a table.** A registry with no rows is its header row plus its separator\n    28|  row and nothing else — never a bare heading, never `- none`, never a sentence saying the\n    29|  section is empty. Counts belong in `summary`.\n    30|- **Ledger citations are allowed anywhere.** `OQ-xxxxxxxx` (eight hex characters) is\n    31|  Stepwise's open-question id. Citing one in a body line, a `source_ref` or a note is what\n    32|  execution-protocol §11.6 requires when a sentence rests on a decision or an open question;\n    33|  it is a cross-reference, not a spec ID, and no id-prefix rule of this template applies\n    34|  to it.\n    35|- **Language:** Generate in DETECTED_LANGUAGE. Section headers in English always.\n    36|\n    37|---\n    38|\n    39|## Spec File Structure\n    40|\n    41|`{project_name}`, `{client_name}`, and `{project_description}` below are the **sanitized** values produced by the Parameter Sanitization step in SKILL.md — newlines, `#`, `|`, and backtick characters stripped, lengths capped. Never substitute the raw extracted values.\n    42|\n    43|The H1 delimiter between `{project_name}` and `PRD Spec` is an EM DASH (U+2014, `—`).\n    44|Not `-`, not `--`, not `–`. Copy the line; do not retype it. The ASCII-only rule in\n    45|execution-protocol §10.3 governs the skeleton's `status: pending` stub string, not this\n    46|title.\n    47|\n    48|```markdown\n    49|# {project_name} — PRD Spec\n    50|version: {NEW_VERSION}\n    51|session: {SESSION_ID}\n    52|mode: {SYNTHESIZE | REPAIR}\n    53|date: {ISO 8601}\n    54|language: {DETECTED_LANGUAGE}\n    55|status: {draft | complete}\n    56|contract_format: structured\n    57|content_hash: {sha256 over canonical PRD-SPEC content excluding this content_hash line}\n    58|\n    59|---\n    60|\n    61|## project_info\n    62|client_name: {client_name}\n    63|project_name: {project_name}\n    64|project_description: {project_description}\n    65|\n    66|---\n    67|\n    68|## scope\n    69|\n    70|### in_scope\n    71|- {scope item 1} | source: {ref} | status: {complete | pending | assumption}\n    72|- {scope item 2} | source: {ref} | status: {complete | pending | assumption}\n    73|\n    74|### out_of_scope\n    75|- {exclusion 1} | source: {ref} | status: {complete | pending | assumption}\n    76|- [PENDING: out_of_scope] | source: {ref} | status: pending\n    77|\n    78|### research_methodology\n    79|- {one-line note on how inputs were gathered/synthesized, e.g. \"derived from project brief analysis; no primary user interviews provided\"} | source: {ref} | status: {complete | pending | assumption}\n    80|\n    81|---\n    82|\n    83|## personas\n    84|\n    85|### P-01: {role_name}\n    86|- type: primary\n    87|- description: {from source}\n    88|- goals: {from source | [PENDING]}\n    89|- pain_points: {from source | [PENDING]}\n    90|- technical_proficiency: {from source | [PENDING]}\n    91|- usage_frequency: {from source | [PENDING]}\n    92|- demographics: {role/seniority}; {technical_proficiency level}; {organizational context — team size or business size where relevant} | source: {ref} | status: {complete | assumption [ASM-XX]}\n    93|- prioritization_rationale: {one-line reason this persona is primary, or [PENDING] on P-02+} | source: {ref} | status: {complete | assumption [ASM-XX]}\n    94|- status: {complete | pending}\n    95|- source: {ref}\n    96|\n    97|### P-02: {role_name}\n    98|- type: secondary\n    99|- description: {from source}\n   100|- goals: {from source | [PENDING]}\n   101|- pain_points: {from source | [PENDING]}\n   102|- technical_proficiency: {from source | [PENDING]}\n   103|- usage_frequency: {from source | [PENDING]}\n   104|- demographics: {role/seniority}; {technical_proficiency level}; {organizational context — team size or business size where relevant} | source: {ref} | status: {complete | assumption [ASM-XX]}\n   105|- status: {complete | pending}\n   106|- source: {ref}\n   107|\n   108|---\n   109|\n   110|## functional_requirements\n   111|\n   112|### FR-01: {requirement_statement}\n   113|- priority: {must_have | should_have | could_have | wont_have | [PENDING]}\n   114|  (MoSCoW/P0–P3 mapping — pick ONE canonical enum value per FR; if the source states a raw\n   115|  MoSCoW or P0–P3 string, translate it and keep the original literal in `literal_registry`:\n   116|  Must Have / P0 → must_have | Should Have / P1 → should_have |\n   117|  Could Have / P2 → could_have | Won't Have / P3 → wont_have)\n   118|- source: {ref}\n   119|- status: {complete | pending}\n   120|- design_note: {mechanism/implementation detail extracted out of the behavioral statement, if any; [PENDING] if none surfaced} | status: {assumption [ASM-XX] | pending}\n   121|- depends_on: [{FR-XX, ...} | none identified]\n   122|- acceptance_criteria:\n   123|  - FR-01-AC-01: given: {precondition} | when: {action} | then: {outcome}\n   124|  - FR-01-AC-02: given: {precondition} | when: {action} | then: {outcome}\n   125|\n   126|### FR-01a: {sub_requirement_statement}\n   127|- parent: FR-01\n   128|- priority: {inherited from parent}\n   129|- source: {ref}\n   130|- status: {complete | pending}\n   131|- design_note: {mechanism/implementation detail extracted out of the behavioral statement, if any; [PENDING] if none surfaced} | status: {assumption [ASM-XX] | pending}\n   132|- depends_on: [{FR-XX, ...} | none identified]\n   133|- acceptance_criteria:\n   134|  - FR-01a-AC-01: given: {precondition} | when: {action} | then: {outcome}\n   135|\n   136|### FR-02: {requirement_statement}\n   137|- priority: {value}\n   138|- source: {ref}\n   139|- status: pending\n   140|- design_note: [PENDING: design_note for FR-02]\n   141|- depends_on: [PENDING: depends_on for FR-02]\n   142|- acceptance_criteria: [PENDING: acceptance_criteria for FR-02]\n   143|\n   144|---\n   145|\n   146|## non_functional_requirements\n   147|\n   148|### NFR-01: {requirement_statement}\n   149|- category: {performance | security | scalability | availability | usability | compliance}\n   150|- target: {numeric_threshold}\n   151|- source: {ref}\n   152|- status: complete\n   153|- design_note: {mechanism/implementation detail extracted out of the requirement statement, if any; [PENDING] if none surfaced} | status: {assumption [ASM-XX] | pending}\n   154|\n   155|### NFR-02: {requirement_statement}\n   156|- category: {category}\n   157|- target: {numeric_threshold} [ASM-01]\n   158|- source: inferred\n   159|- status: assumption\n   160|- design_note: {mechanism/implementation detail extracted out of the requirement statement, if any; [PENDING] if none surfaced} | status: {assumption [ASM-XX] | pending}\n   161|\n   162|### NFR-03: {requirement_statement}\n   163|- category: {category}\n   164|- target: [PENDING: nfr_target]\n   165|- source: {ref}\n   166|- status: pending\n   167|- design_note: [PENDING: design_note for NFR-03]\n   168|\n   169|---\n   170|\n   171|## kpis\n   172|\n   173|### KPI-01: {description}\n   174|- target: {numeric_value}\n   175|- measurement: {how collected}\n   176|- timeframe: {when measured}\n   177|- source: {ref}\n   178|- status: {complete | pending}\n   179|\n   180|---\n   181|\n   182|## jtbd\n   183|\n   184|### JTBD-01: core_functional\n   185|- situation: {from source}\n   186|- motivation: {from source}\n   187|- outcome: {from source}\n   188|- source: {ref}\n   189|- status: {complete | pending}\n   190|\n   191|### JTBD-02: related\n   192|- situation: {from source}\n   193|- motivation: {from source}\n   194|- outcome: {from source}\n   195|- source: {ref}\n   196|- status: {complete | pending}\n   197|\n   198|---\n   199|\n   200|## traceability\n   201|\n   202|| FR | fr_name | JTBD | jtbd_name | direction | status |\n   203||----|---------|------|-----------|-----------|--------|\n   204|| FR-01 | {requirement_statement, short} | JTBD-01 | {job statement, short} | forward | mapped |\n   205|| FR-02 | {requirement_statement, short} | — | — | forward | orphan |\n   206|| — | — | JTBD-03 | {job statement, short} | reverse | unsatisfied |\n   207|\n   208|`fr_name` and `jtbd_name` are copied from the `### FR-XX:` and `### JTBD-XX:` headings.\n   209|An `—` in a name cell is valid only where its id cell is also `—`. This is the one table\n   210|a reviewer reads to judge coverage, and a grid of bare ids cannot be judged.\n   211|\n   212|---\n   213|\n   214|## dependencies\n   215|\n   216|### DEP-01: {dependency_name}\n   217|- type: {external | internal | technical}\n   218|- description: {what it is}\n   219|- owner: {who owns it | [PENDING]}\n   220|- impact_if_unavailable: {consequence}\n   221|- source: {ref}\n   222|- status: {complete | pending}\n   223|\n   224|### inter_feature_dependencies\n   225|- {FR-XX depends_on FR-YY: one-line reason} | source: {ref} | status: {complete | pending | assumption}\n   226|- inter_feature_dependencies: none identified | source: {ref} | status: complete\n   227|  (use this exact line, unmodified, when no cross-FR dependency exists — see each FR's own\n   228|  `depends_on` field in `functional_requirements` for the per-FR detail this section rolls up)\n   229|\n   230|---\n   231|\n   232|## risks\n   233|\n   234|### RSK-01: {risk_statement}\n   235|- likelihood: {high | medium | low | [PENDING]}\n   236|- impact: {high | medium | low | [PENDING]}\n   237|- mitigation: {strategy}\n   238|- source: {ref}\n   239|- status: {complete | pending}\n   240|\n   241|---\n   242|\n   243|## assumptions\n   244|\n   245|### ASM-01: {assumption_statement}\n   246|- impact_if_wrong: {consequence}\n   247|- source_basis: {ref | inferred from ...}\n   248|- status: active\n   249|\n   250|---\n   251|\n   252|## constraints\n   253|\n   254|Sub-categories `budget`, `timeline`, `resource`, and `regulatory` are MANDATORY — each MUST\n   255|have at least one entry (or the `\"unknown — stakeholder input required\"` pending placeholder).\n   256|`organizational` and any other sub-category are additive, not a substitute for the four\n   257|mandatory ones.\n   258|\n   259|### budget\n   260|- {constraint 1} | source: {ref} | status: {complete | pending}\n   261|- [PENDING: budget_constraints] | value: \"unknown — stakeholder input required\" | status: pending\n   262|\n   263|### timeline\n   264|- {constraint 1, expressed as phase gate or relative sequencing — never a calendar date} | source: {ref} | status: {complete | pending}\n   265|- [PENDING: timeline_constraints] | value: \"unknown — stakeholder input required\" | status: pending\n   266|\n   267|### resource\n   268|- {constraint 1} | source: {ref} | status: {complete | pending}\n   269|- [PENDING: resource_constraints] | value: \"unknown — stakeholder input required\" | status: pending\n   270|\n   271|### regulatory\n   272|- {constraint 1} | source: {ref}\n   273|- [PENDING: regulatory_constraints] | status: pending\n   274|\n   275|### organizational\n   276|- {constraint 1} | source: {ref}\n   277|\n   278|---\n   279|\n   280|## mvp_phasing\n   281|\n   282|Every line in this section is an item, so every line carries `source` and `status` like any\n   283|other item. A phase with no members is written `- none | source: {ref} | status: complete` —\n   284|never an empty heading.\n   285|\n   286|The priority label leads the line so the parentheses are free to carry names. This is the\n   287|section a Product Owner reads as the roadmap; a phase listed as bare ids tells them nothing\n   288|about what ships when.\n   289|\n   290|### phase_1_mvp\n   291|- must_have: FR-01 ({name}), FR-03 ({name}), FR-05 ({name}) | source: {ref} | status: {complete | pending | assumption}\n   292|\n   293|### phase_2\n   294|- should_have: FR-02 ({name}), FR-06 ({name}) | source: {ref} | status: {complete | pending | assumption}\n   295|\n   296|### phase_3\n   297|- could_have: FR-04 ({name}), FR-07 ({name}) | source: {ref} | status: {complete | pending | assumption}\n   298|\n   299|### deferred\n   300|- wont_have: FR-08 ({name}) | source: {ref} | status: {complete | pending | assumption}\n   301|\n   302|### sequencing_notes\n   303|- FR-03 ({name}) requires DEP-01 ({dependency_name}) resolved before start | source: {ref} | status: {complete | pending | assumption}\n   304|- FR-06 ({name}) depends on FR-01 ({name}) completion | source: {ref} | status: {complete | pending | assumption}\n   305|\n   306|---\n   307|\n   308|## literal_registry\n   309|\n   310|Typed literal registry for exact values downstream research/planning must preserve.\n   311|Include only literals explicitly present in source material: enum members, error\n   312|codes, route strings, field names, precision/range values, storage keys, event\n   313|names, and source-backed positive/negative technology constraints.\n   314|\n   315|| id | name | exact_value | type | applies_to_ids | source_ref |\n   316||----|------|-------------|------|----------------|------------|\n   317|| LIT-01 | {literal_name} | {exact value} | {enum | error_code | route | field | range | constraint | other} | {FR-XX, FR-XX-AC-YY, NFR-XX} | {stable section/ID anchor} |\n   318|\n   319|---\n   320|\n   321|## glossary\n   322|\n   323|| term_id | term | definition | first_used | source_ref |\n   324||---------|------|------------|------------|------------|\n   325|| TERM-01 | {term} | {definition} | {section/ID} | {stable section/ID anchor} |\n   326|\n   327|---\n   328|\n   329|## open_questions\n   330|\n   331|This section is the **single consolidated registry** of all unresolved items.\n   332|Every `[PENDING]` marker, every `orphan` traceability entry, every `assumption`\n   333|that needs validation — all appear here once.\n   334|\n   335|Downstream skills (Epics, User Stories, Architecture, Implementation) read\n   336|ONLY this section to understand what is unresolved. They do NOT scan other\n   337|sections for [PENDING] markers — this registry IS the source of truth.\n   338|\n   339|### pending_inputs\n   340|\n   341|| id | affected_ids | blocking | type | section | item_id | field | impact | question | fallback_behavior | source_ref |\n   342||----|--------------|----------|------|---------|---------|-------|--------|----------|-------------------|------------|\n   343|| PI-01 | {P-01} | {yes | no} | missing | personas | P-01 | pain_points | {HIGH | MEDIUM | LOW} | {needed answer} | {BLOCKED or narrowest safe behavior} | {stable section/ID anchor} |\n   344|| PI-02 | {FR-02, FR-02-AC-*} | yes | missing | functional_requirements | FR-02 | acceptance_criteria | HIGH | {needed answer} | BLOCKED | {stable section/ID anchor} |\n   345|| PI-03 | {NFR-03} | {yes | no} | missing | non_functional_requirements | NFR-03 | target | {HIGH | MEDIUM | LOW} | {needed answer} | {fallback threshold or BLOCKED} | {stable section/ID anchor} |\n   346|\n   347|### traceability_gaps\n   348|\n   349|| id | affected_ids | blocking | direction | fr_id | jtbd_id | impact | note | fallback_behavior | source_ref |\n   350||----|--------------|----------|-----------|-------|---------|--------|------|-------------------|------------|\n   351|| TG-01 | {FR-02} | {yes | no} | forward | FR-02 | — | {HIGH | MEDIUM | LOW} | Orphan FR: no JTBD served | {research may proceed with explicit orphan note or BLOCKED} | {stable section/ID anchor} |\n   352|| TG-02 | {JTBD-03} | {yes | no} | reverse | — | JTBD-03 | {HIGH | MEDIUM | LOW} | Unsatisfied JTBD: no implementing FR | {defer JTBD or BLOCKED} | {stable section/ID anchor} |\n   353|\n   354|### assumptions_to_validate\n   355|\n   356|| id | affected_ids | blocking | assumption | impact_if_wrong | validation_method | fallback_behavior | source_ref |\n   357||----|--------------|----------|------------|-----------------|-------------------|-------------------|------------|\n   358|| ASM-01 | {FR-XX, NFR-YY} | {yes | no} | {statement} | {consequence} | {how to confirm/deny} | {narrowest safe behavior or BLOCKED} | {stable section/ID anchor} |\n   359|\n   360|All three tables above render with their full column sets even when they hold zero rows:\n   361|header row + separator row, example rows deleted. A spec with no traceability gaps still\n   362|carries the `traceability_gaps` heading and its ten-column header. Report the zero in\n   363|`summary`, not by omitting the table.\n   364|\n   365|### summary\n   366|- total_frs: {N}\n   367|- total_nfrs: {N}\n   368|- total_jtbds: {N}\n   369|- total_kpis: {N}\n   370|- pending_inputs: {N}\n   371|- traceability_gaps: {N}\n   372|- assumptions: {N}\n   373|- risks: {N}\n   374|- dependencies: {N}\n   375|- status: {draft | complete}\n   376|```\n   377|\n   378|---\n   379|\n   380|## Generation Rules\n   381|\n   382|### Section Ordering\n   383|Generate sections in the order shown above. This order reflects dependency flow:\n   384|scope → personas → FRs → NFRs → KPIs → JTBDs → traceability → deps → risks →\n   385|assumptions → constraints → mvp_phasing → literal_registry → glossary → open_questions.\n   386|\n   387|The traceability section MUST come after both FRs and JTBDs are generated.\n   388|The open_questions section is ALWAYS LAST — it consolidates from all prior sections.\n   389|\n   390|### Consolidation Pass (Before Writing)\n   391|After generating all sections, perform a single consolidation pass:\n   392|1. Scan every section for items with status: pending → create PI-XX in open_questions —\n   393|   ONE row per DECISION the project needs, never one per unfilled field: several items\n   394|   missing the same descriptive field collapse into at most one question (or none), and a\n   395|   field the inputs never mention is `not stated in inputs`, not a pending input\n   396|   (SKILL.md Status Protocol; execution-protocol.md §11.6 \"A template field is not a question\")\n   397|2. Scan traceability for orphan/unsatisfied → create TG-XX in open_questions\n   398|3. Scan assumptions → create entry in assumptions_to_validate\n   399|4. Compute summary counts\n   400|5. Set top-level status: `complete` if zero pending_inputs AND zero traceability_gaps.\n</file>","isError":false,"durationMs":8}}
