[08:25:54] {"type":"tool_end","payload":{"toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-b0bbc836b28e5936","toolName":"read","result":"<file path=\"C:\\IA Trainings\\CalcService\\.coda\\skills\\researching-prd\\references\\spec-template.md\" lines=\"432\" start=\"400\" end=\"431\" returned=\"32\" has_more=\"true\" truncated=\"false\">\n   400|5. Set top-level status: `complete` if zero pending_inputs AND zero traceability_gaps.\n   401|   Otherwise: `draft`.\n   402|6. Compute `content_hash` by RUNNING the recipe in `execution-protocol.md`\n   403|   §10.5.4 — as the LAST write, after every section is final. You cannot compute a\n   404|   sha256 yourself, and a hand-written 64-hex string fails the verifier about\n   405|   three times in four — unpredictably, which is worse than always. Write the\n   406|   placeholder of 64 zeros, run the script, done. Never use mtime.\n   407|\n   408|### Structured Contract Rules\n   409|- Native PRDs emitted by this skill declare `contract_format: structured`.\n   410|- Acceptance criteria IDs are globally stable: `FR-XX-AC-YY`.\n   411|- `literal_registry` is authoritative only when complete. If a source-backed\n   412|  literal appears in FR/NFR/JTBD prose, acceptance criteria, constraints, or\n   413|  glossary, it must appear in `literal_registry`.\n   414|- `open_questions` rows use `affected_ids`, `blocking`, and `fallback_behavior`.\n   415|  If `blocking: yes`, `fallback_behavior` is `BLOCKED` unless source material\n   416|  explicitly supplies a safe fallback.\n   417|- Source references use stable section/ID anchors, not line numbers.\n   418|\n   419|### REPAIR Mode\n   420|- Load existing spec file\n   421|- Apply REPAIR_DIRECTIVES to targeted sections\n   422|- Recalculate traceability (full rebuild if FRs or JTBDs changed)\n   423|- Rebuild open_questions from scratch (always reflects current state)\n   424|- Increment version, log changes\n   425|\n   426|### Bias Detection (During Generation)\n   427|Apply inline — do not generate a separate bias report:\n   428|- Technology name not in source → rewrite as capability need\n   429|- Architecture decision without source → mark as ASM-XX\n   430|- Implementation detail in FR → move to notes field on that FR\n   431|- Vendor name in dependency without source → mark as ASM-XX\n</file>","isError":false,"durationMs":6}}
