[08:32:59] {"type":"thinking_delta","payload":{"delta":"The full spec is on disk and reads correctly. Quality gate checks:\n\n1. Source Fidelity: every FR/NFR has a source or is pending/assumption — NFR-06 has \"source: not stated in inputs\" and status pending — OK.\n2. Zero Invention: all complete items have sources — OK.\n3. Traceability: all FRs mapped, no orphans — OK.\n4. NFR targets: numeric or pending — OK.\n5. ACs: every FR has ≥1 AC — OK.\n6. Bias check: no technology names not in sources — H2 appears in LIT-11 sourced from the brief's alignment note (\"H2-based lightweight persistence strategy\") — that IS in the source. OK.\n7. open_questions: every pending/orphan/assumption appears exactly once — pending items: FR-03 design_note (PI-01), FR-08 (PI-02), NFR-01 (PI-03), NFR-04 (PI-04), NFR-05 (PI-05), NFR-06 (PI-06), NFR-07 (PI-07), KPI-05/06/07 (PI-08), DEP-01 (PI-09), constraints budget/timeline/resource (PI-10), regulatory (PI-11). Assumptions ASM-01..07 in assumptions_to_validate. DEP-01 status pending → covered by PI-09. OK.\n8. ID consistency: FR-01..10, NFR-01..07, KPI-01..07, JTBD-01..04, DEP-01..02, RSK-01..04, ASM-01..07, PI-01..11, LIT-01..11, TERM-01..09 — no gaps/dups. OK.\n9. Structured contract: contract_format: structured present, AC IDs FR-XX-AC-YY, enriched open_questions. OK.\n10. Hash contract: need to run the sha256 script.\n\nOne remaining issue: NFR-01 target line has a trailing space after \"[PENDING: exact numeric threshold] \" — harmless.\n\nAlso check: no calendar references. The spec has \"date: 2026-10-28\" in header (that's the header field, required by template). \"timeframe: not stated in inputs\" — fine. No week/month references in content. The template requires the date header, so that's fine.\n\nNow Step 5: write AUDIT file, compute content_hash, then LAST ACTION _progress.json COMPLETED, Memory Bank writes, guidance check, sidecar.\n\nOrder per §11.4: outputs verified → Memory Bank writes → _progress.json COMPLETED → sidecar → final response. And content_hash is \"the LAST write before the §11 sidecar\" per §10.5.4 — actually it says \"as the LAST write, after every section is final\". The hash script edits SPEC_FILE. So: write audit (with final hash value reported), run hash script, then memory bank, then progress COMPLETED, then sidecar.\n\nWait — audit needs the final content_hash value. So run hash script first, then write audit with the digest, then memory bank, then progress, then sidecar.\n\nAlso §2.1 pre-completion self-validation gate before LAST ACTION.\n\nLet me run the hash script now. Note: python3 may not exist on Windows; try python. The script is the sanctioned exception. Let me use python (Windows often has `python`). I'll try python3 first, fallback python.","turnId":"2ac21793-967e-44e9-9b2c-0c115fe85b62"}}
[08:32:59] {"type":"message_delta","payload":{"delta":"Full spec verified on disk — all 16 sections populated, IDs consistent, registries complete. **Step 5 — outputs:** computing the `content_hash` by running the §10.5.4 recipe (never hand-written).","turnId":"2ac21793-967e-44e9-9b2c-0c115fe85b62"}}
[08:32:59] {"type":"tool_start","payload":{"toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-bc2328fb2adb0556","toolName":"bash","args":{"command":"cd \"C:\\IA Trainings\\CalcService\" && (python3 - \"artifacts/outputs/product-definition/prd/PRD-SPEC-pd-20261027-calc001.md\" <<'EOF'\nimport hashlib, re, sys\npath = sys.argv[1]\ntext = open(path, encoding='utf-8').read()\nm = re.search(r'^content_hash:\\s*([0-9a-f]{64})\\s*\\n?', text, re.M)\nif not m:\n    sys.exit('content_hash line missing or not 64 hex characters')\ncanonical = text[:m.start()] + text[m.end():]\ndigest = hashlib.sha256(canonical.encode('utf-8')).hexdigest()\nopen(path, 'w', encoding='utf-8').write(\n    text[:m.start()] + f'content_hash: {digest}\\n' + text[m.end():]\n)\nprint(digest)\nEOF\n) 2>/dev/null || (python - \"artifacts/outputs/product-definition/prd/PRD-SPEC-pd-20261027-calc001.md\" <<'EOF'\nimport hashlib, re, sys\npath = sys.argv[1]\ntext = open(path, encoding='utf-8').read()\nm = re.search(r'^content_hash:\\s*([0-9a-f]{64})\\s*\\n?', text, re.M)\nif not m:\n    sys.exit('content_hash line missing or not 64 hex characters')\ncanonical = text[:m.start()] + text[m.end():]\ndigest = hashlib.sha256(canonical.encode('utf-8')).hexdigest()\nopen(path, 'w', encoding='utf-8').write(\n    text[:m.start()] + f'content_hash: {digest}\\n' + text[m.end():]\n)\nprint(digest)\nEOF\n)","timeout":30000,"working_directory":"C:\\IA Trainings\\CalcService","description":"Compute and write sha256 content_hash into PRD spec","background":false}}}
